From d1dc7e15498f30cb65553abd31c96653fcc04996 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Senior Matthew <SeniorMatt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 14:20:11 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 10/25] kcm_icons: theme list read after the first frame,
 previews staggered, empty and busy states
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Page type: Gallery (docs/page-design.md section 5). Config key (kdeglobals Icons/Theme), pending deletion, KNS, install from
file and the preview rendering code are unchanged. NOT BUILT YET (owner stopped heavy work); checked statically only.

Moved / renamed: nothing visible changed in wording: Install from File… and Get New… were already page actions top right,
per-theme Remove stays a GridDelegate action. There are no icon-size options in this KCM in master (kcm_icons rows: Theme,
Install, Get New, Remove only), so no sub-page was needed. New: "No icon themes found" empty state, busy indicator only
after 150 ms. Relabel table: inventory/relabel/kcm_icons.tsv (outer repo). Inventory --strict: 4 rows ok, 0 lost.
HIG ids: HIG-001, HIG-006; page-design sections 5, 7.

Speed (cause found in code, not measured):
- IconModule::load() ran IconsModel::load() synchronously: KIconTheme::list() then one KIconTheme (index.theme read and
  parse) per installed theme (iconsmodel.cpp load()), plus QFileInfo writability checks, before the page existed.
  Now load() queues it one event-loop turn later (generation counter, new property IconModule.loaded); the grid has no
  model until loaded.
- Every card rendered its six preview icons in Component.onCompleted via Qt.callLater (previewIcons: KIconTheme, PNG/SVG
  loads per icon, main thread), all in the same turn. Now a Timer per card, 30 ms + 40 ms * min(index, 11), so frames keep
  coming. Widgets/pixmaps stay on the main thread: this spreads the cost, it does not remove it.
- After numbers: pending, manager will measure.

Not built yet; uncertain: that `index` resolves inside the Flow's Timer (delegate context property, should); the
unchanged downstream callers of IconsModel::load() (installThemes) still run it synchronously on purpose.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
